This Makejail is designed to be run by [Overlord](https://github.com/DtxdF/overlord) and supports only one virtual machine per jail. For this reason, in the remaining examples, you'll see deployment files intended for use with Overlord.

### Networking

Before you begin, keep in mind that this Makejail relies on [Virtual Networks](https://appjail.readthedocs.io/en/latest/getting-started/#virtual-networks). Inside the jail, NAT is used with a `192.168.8.0/24` network, with `192.168.8.1` as the gateway, so you can use any IPv4 address within your virtual machine that falls within that range. I recommend using `192.168.8.2/24`.

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Jail                                                                  |
|                                                                       |
|       +-----------------+                                             |
|       | if_epair(4):    |          +-------------------------+        |
| ----> | 10.0.0.5        | -------> | NAT: 192.168.8.0/24     |        |
| <---- |                 |          +-------------------------+        |
|       +-----------------+                       ^                     |
|                                                 |                     |
|                                                 v                     |
|                                       +-------------------------+     |
|                                       | if_bridge(4):           |     |
|                                       | 192.168.8.1             |     |
|                                       +-------------------------+     |
|                                                 ^                     |
|                                                 |                     |
|                                                 v                     |
|                                           +-------------+             |
|                                           | if_tap(4)   |             |
|                                           +-------------+             |
|                                                 ^                     |
|                                                 |                     |
|       +-----------------------------------------v-------------------+ |
|       | VM                                                          | |
|       |                                                             | |
|       |       +---------------------------------------------------+ | |
|       |       | if_vnet(4):                                       | | |
|       |       | - inet: 192.168.8.2/24                            | | |
|       |       | - defaultrouter: 192.168.8.1                      | | |
|       |       +---------------------------------------------------+ | |
|       +-------------------------------------------------------------+ |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Basic usage

**windows10.yaml**:

```yaml
kind: vmJail
datacenters:
  main:
    entrypoint: !ENV '${ENTRYPOINT}'
    access_token: !ENV '${TOKEN}'
deployIn:
  labels:
    - desktop
vmName: 'windows10'
makejail: 'gh+AppJail-makejails/windows10'
overwrite: true
options:
  - fstab: '/var/local-os /vm/.iso nullfs ro'
  - fstab: '/var/appjail-vm/windows10 /media'
build-arguments:
  - is_public_vm: '1'
  - exclude_ports: '5900'
template:
  loader: 'uefi'
  cpu: '4'
  memory: '4G'
  graphics: 'yes'
  graphics_listen: '0.0.0.0'
  graphics_res: '1280x720'
  graphics_wait: 'no'
  xhci_mouse: 'yes'
  network0_type: 'virtio-net'
  network0_switch: 'public'
  network0_mac: '10:e7:c6:66:f8:c7'
  utctime: 'NO'
  wired_memory: 'YES'
  uefi_vars: 'YES'
  debug: 'YES'
  disk1_type: 'nvme'
  disk1_dev: 'custom'
  disk1_name: '/media/data.img'
  disk2_type: 'ahci-cd'
  disk2_dev: 'custom'
  disk2_name: '/vm/.iso/virtio-win.iso'
  virt_console0: 'org.qemu.guest_agent.0'
diskLayout:
  driver: 'nvme'
  size: '30G'
  from:
    type: 'iso'
    isoFile: 'es-es_windows_10_enterprise_ltsc_2021_x64_dvd_51d721ea.iso'
```

**.env**:

```dotenv
ENTRYPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8888
TOKEN=invalid_token
